00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:48.749
Part 2.

96
00:06:49.029 --> 00:06:50.906
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

97
00:06:52.156 --> 00:06:53.073
Intuition.

98
00:06:53.353 --> 00:06:54.847
The tail is the product.

99
00:06:55.127 --> 00:07:08.524
If a page needs 20 services and each is fast 99% of the time, the page is fast only 0.99²⁰ about 82% of the time, nearly one in five requests hits someone's bad moment.

100
00:07:08.804 --> 00:07:12.196
Speeding up the common case doesn't help; you must cut the tail.

101
00:07:12.476 --> 00:07:13.308
(L1).

102
00:07:13.588 --> 00:07:15.337
A busy queue is a traffic jam.

103
00:07:15.617 --> 00:07:21.825
At 50% utilization there's slack; at 95% a small burst backs everything up.

104
00:07:22.105 --> 00:07:27.012
Latency doesn't rise gently to a wall, it curves sharply near 100%.

105
00:07:27.292 --> 00:07:31.068
Running efficiently at 90% is running on the cliff edge.

106
00:07:31.348 --> 00:07:32.372
(L1 C).

107
00:07:33.722 --> 00:07:35.642
Profiling is turning on the lights.

108
00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:40.957
Optimizing by intuition is fixing what you think is slow; a profiler shows what is.

109
00:07:41.237 --> 00:07:45.930
It's routinely a surprise, a logging call, a string concat, a needless copy.

110
00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.085
(L3).

111
00:07:47.365 --> 00:07:49.455
The GC is a background tax.

112
00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:56.370
Most of the time it's invisible; occasionally it stops the world for a pause that lands in your p99.

113
00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:59.509
Which collector you pick decides how big that pause is.

114
00:07:59.789 --> 00:08:00.621
(L2).

115
00:08:01.971 --> 00:08:04.253
Tail latency and why it compounds.

116
00:08:04.533 --> 00:08:13.963
From Dean and Barroso's The Tail at Scale: in a system that fans out to many components and waits for all of them, the slowest component sets the latency.

117
00:08:14.243 --> 00:08:26.659
If each backend is slow (say p95) 5% of the time, then across N backends the chance that at least one is slow is 1 minus 0.95ᴺ.

